KG42.register("source_edge_archive-2f746d8027683be5bb64acd7",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::E::v141-c-R007-E002","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG40-12aedc3eec573697","target":"COMP-ffbf050cce03a2e6","source_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","source_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"680eaf066f2ba21fbace9fb4ca77b41d105beb2298faab362c48b8cb8ebf2460","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Sell orders may be submitted via participants' EMTS; each order includes an order quantity and price. Scope: BMG virtual market: described order-submission arrangement for prosumers and consumers. Condition: Participants are willing to trade electricity in the next time slot. Prosumers submit supply bids at the minimum price limit they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market. Scope: BMG bidding strategy implemented at the time described. The feed-in tariff sets residents' price limit for selling energy under the stated economic-interest condition. Scope: General microgrid market framework: residents' selling-price limits. Condition: Residents are interested in participating only for economic reasons.","target_definition":"Submitted buy orders, which include requested quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders. Submitted sell orders, which include offered quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted sell orders, which include offered quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R007-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish general microgrid design, the BMG implemented virtual double auction, and the example EMTS; the original undercut statement is recorded as a source statement and is not rewritten on our own into the opposite condition."}});
